+# Tool Input Validation
+
+| Field  | Value                |
+| ------ | -------------------- |
+| Issue  | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
+| Status | Draft                |
+
+`ToolRegistry.execute` validates the caller's input against the tool's declared JSON Schema before invoking the executor. Invalid input is returned to the model as a `ToolResponse` without reaching executor code, so a malformed call becomes something the model can read and correct within the existing tool-round budget.
+
+## Validation Behaviour
+
+- `execute` validates `input` against the tool's `inputSchema` before calling the executor; when the input fails the check, the executor is not invoked and the method returns a `ToolResponse` whose `result` names the failing field ([validated by: returns a ToolResponse naming the missing required field without calling the executor](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L4)).
+- When input is rejected, the returned `result` text names the failing property path and the violated constraint, and does not contain the offending input value ([validated by: rejects a wrong-typed field without exposing the submitted value](../../src/orchestration/tools/registry.acceptance.test.ts#L27)).
